  "verified": [
    "2026-09-06: fan rows chain rear to front with the SL-Infinity template rotated pi on both rows",
    "2026-09-06: GPU bar LED 0 at the rear; Prism S GPU strimer rotated 180 from the naive placement",
    "2026-09-06: both Nollie strimers need a rows-only flip; the 24-pin ribbon must sit at the keyed end of the LIAN LI MB socket",
    "2026-09-06: TL LCD fan rings wind counter-clockwise as seen from the glass in this mount"
  ],
  "unverified": [
    "TL fan LEDs share the named LCD centers: fan/LCD 1 middle, 2 top, 3 bottom on the side radiator. Physical receiver-to-fan identity still needs a hardware check.",
    "DRAM 0x71 is the stick nearer the CPU",
    "2026-09-07: Corsair LED zones rotated +pi/2 after a horizontal sweep traveled top to bottom; direction awaits visual confirmation."
  ],
  "geometry_sources": [
    {
      "url": "https://gitlab.com/signalrgb/signal-plugins/-/blob/091e3f149cbc06ab4ea0f575cb537a7ddb01df17/Plugins/Corsair/Modern_Corsair/Corsair_ICUE_Link_Hub.js",
      "notes": "LINK H150i positions divided by 6 (16 perimeter LEDs then 4 inner LEDs); LINK LCD positions divided by 16 (24 LEDs). Both maps retain device LED order. Placement rotation is specific to this rig. These SignalRGB maps differ from the auto-layout hints in crates/hypercolor-hal/src/drivers/corsair/types.rs: the HAL AIO perimeter starts at the rightmost point and its inner group starts right, while SignalRGB starts the perimeter below right and the inner group at the top. The HAL LCD ring starts right, while SignalRGB starts near bottom left (its LED 17 is rightmost). Hardware reconciliation remains unverified; this rig overrides those hints."
    }
  ]
